CompressBeta -- CompressBeta is an option for eagon, default is true
********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        E = eagon(R,b,CompressBeta =>bool1, Verbose =>bool2)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
      * b, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * bool1, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 
      * bool2, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 
  * Outputs:
      * E, an instance of the type *note EagonData: EagonData,, 

Description
===========

eagonBeta(E,i) := E#{"eagonBeta",n,0} is defined by lifting another map along
the map dVert^n_i. If CompressBeta => true, the default, then the lifting uses
the smallest initial subsequence of the blocks of source dVert as possible, and
thus the columns of picture eagonBeta(E,i) will have fewer nonzero entries. if
Verbose =>true, then data about the usage is printed.

