DisplayBlocks -- Display => "DisplayBlocks" option for picture
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        N = picture(M, Display => "DisplayBlocks")
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
  * Outputs:
      * N, a *note net: (Macaulay2Doc)Net,, prints a "picture" -- a net --
        showing information about the blocks

Description
===========

The free modules that are the sources and targets of the matrices defined in
the EagonData eagon(R,b) generally have many components. These can be analyzed
with the functions *note picture: picture,, and *note mapComponent:
mapComponent,. Each summand of one of these free modules has a label of the
form (i, {u_1..u_s}) representing the tensor product K_i **
X_{u_1}**..**X_{u_s}, where 0\leq i \leq numvars R and 1\leq u_t \leq
projective dimension R. Thus a block is identified by a pair of such symbols,
representing source and target.

Display => "picture"; with this option, *note picture: picture, does not
actually print the entries of the matrices. But picture(M, Display =>
"DisplayBlocks") prints a net with the matrices themselves.

