mapComponent -- extract a single component from a labeled map
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        N = mapComponent(M,tar,src)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, labeled map from eagon(R,b)
      * tar, a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, symbol of a free module
        components of the Eagon resolution
      * src, a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, symbol of a free module
        components of the Eagon resolution
  * Outputs:
      * N, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 

Description
===========

The source and target of a a map in the Eagon double complex, such as dVert,
dHor, and eagonBeta, are direct sums of tensor products of the form
K_i**X_{u_1}**..**X_{u_s} where K_i is a term of the Koszul complex and X_i is
a term of the S-free resolution of R, all tensored with R. This tensor product
is represented by a symbol that is a two element Sequence

(i, \{u_1..u_s\})

The block structure of the matrix, together with the source and target
Sequences, can be seen from picture M.

The function mapComponent returns a single block.

