picture -- information about components of a labeled Matrix or Complex
**********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        N = picture M
        L = picture C
        L = picture E
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
      * C, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, 
      * E, an instance of the type *note EagonData: EagonData,, produced by
        eagon; picture E is equivalent to picture *note eagonResolution:
        eagonResolution, E and to picture res E
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Display => ..., default value "picture"
      * Transpose => ..., default value false
      * Verbose => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * N, a *note net: (Macaulay2Doc)Net,, 
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, List of Nets, one for each map in
        the complex

Description
===========

The free modules that are the sources and targets of the matrices defined in
the EagonData eagon(R,b) generally have many components. These can be analyzed
with the functions picture, and *note mapComponent: mapComponent,. Each summand
of one of these free modules has a label of the form (i, \{u_1..u_s\})
representing the tensor product K_i ** X_{u_1}**..**X_{u_s}, where 0\leq i \leq
numvars R and 1\leq u_t \leq projective dimension over S of R. Thus a block is
identified by a pair of such symbols in the order target, source.

For any labeled matrix M, picture M (with the default option Display =>
"picture") prints a net showing which blocks of the matrix are 0 (represented
by .); or nonzero and in the maximal ideal, represented by *; or contain a unit
entry, represented by a pair of numbers, which are the rank of the target of
the matrix and the rank of the matrix tensored with the residue field (the
"nonminimal part").

Options: The default option is Display => "picture". With the option
Display=>"DisplayBlocks", picture prints the matrices in each block. With any
other assignment such as Display =>"", Display prints the whole matrix, without
showing the block structure. With the option Verbose => true, picture prints
(numrows,numcols) for each block. With the option Transpose => true, picture
prints the data for the transposed matrix (possibly useful if there are many
columns in the matrix).

Applied to a complex of labeled matrices such as that produced by (res,
EagonData) or applied to an instance of EagonData, picture prints a netList of
the pictures of the maps in the complex



