verticalStrand -- extracts one vertical strand from an Eagon double complex
***************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        F = verticalStrand(E,i)
  * Inputs:
      * E, an instance of the type *note EagonData: EagonData,, produced by
        eagon(R,b)
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, which strand
  * Outputs:
      * F, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, beginning of the free
        resolution of the i-th boundary module of the Koszul complex

Description
===========

The 0-th vertical strand is the Koszul complex of R. The vertical strands are
never resolutions unless R is regular. The key lemma in Eagon's treatment
identifies the i-th homology H_i of the n-th vertical strand with H_0**X_i.

